<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Chancellor Merz seeks CDU support as AfD encroaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:682bd89c9f4b808c432f4d712c00dd634aadddf2c125c8623090b067334786d5</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-seeks-cdu-support-as-afd-encroaches/a-79290192--ce473c897283.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-seeks-cdu-support-as-afd-encroaches/a-79290192?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the CDU's crushing defeat in the Saxony-Anhalt state election, many are expressing doubts about the party's leader, Chancellor Friedrich Merz. But the CDU doesn't appear to have a viable alternative.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Oktoberfest beer prices rise, outpacing inflation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7173a22477b368527ddf6b1425f35cb7168262d92a602542e3b01da63594353d</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T18:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-oktoberfest-beer-prices-rise-outpacing-inflation/a-79296932--12fa98bb1113.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-oktoberfest-beer-prices-rise-outpacing-inflation/a-79296932?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest's traditional beer mug, the Mass, will cost an average of €15.61 ($18.50) at this year's festival in Munich.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Conservative state premiers rally behind Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c4314d46bf8ee93b5ce4d63c127d476d93f7b7b336df29d30e2953c5ec4394e</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-conservative-state-premiers-rally-behind-merz/live-79289786--e3b9d59d079d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-conservative-state-premiers-rally-behind-merz/live-79289786?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">All eight CDU state premiers have backed Friedrich Merz, urging the party to focus on rebuilding trust. Plus, Germany's coalition is weighing rapid relief as record fuel prices pile pressure on households.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz to cancel UN trip amid party infighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae908fbc286bcc3a1624d7eb14693cce07d58426175e79a3ac1b7f92f9d3a645</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-to-cancel-un-trip-over-party-infighting/live-79273324--971a6ac4ea62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-to-cancel-un-trip-amid-party-infighting/live-79273324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's chancellor nixxed his trip over doubts about his leadership after party losses to the AfD in state elections. Meanwhile, Defense Minister Pistorius is in Washington for talks with his US counterpart.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After Neuer: Who will be Germany's new No. 1 goalkeeper?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdceb39828c2cb4a3025cf3ceb2e2241a97e77fe3e58611e36a3af7f1b917f68</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377--1d35484fc587.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following Manuel Neuer's retirement, there are many candidates to succeed him, but which goalkeeper will Jürgen Klopp choose? What factors will play a role? And will Neuer's future have an indirect influence?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German drama 'Blindspot Berlin' revisits 2016 Christmas market attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f1b222ffff1c89e5c21bfa26068d71dd4c2f3b181d51ba31cdcbffcf6d9fa4f</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162--11e3e3b69ad1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-drama-blindspot-berlin-revisits-2016-christmas-market-attack/a-79281162?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A decade after the terrorist attack on a Berlin Christmas market, a new German miniseries looks into the institutional failures that allowed the deadly truck rampage to happen.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Drivers in Germany fume over soaring fuel prices</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a23a45c1a7548e19eeb823d39974b8e23e2c05c97642afa0af160148b8ac7220</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/drivers-in-germany-fume-over-soaring-fuel-prices/a-79282456--6a933389e322.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/drivers-in-germany-fume-over-soaring-fuel-prices/a-79282456?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz wants to provide relief to motorists. But exactly how this is to happen remains unclear.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Holocaust survivor on 'very dangerous' AfD Saxony-Anhalt win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf83139c54b0c83d756860740f8689276d156d8360f770b9a68acff6ce45f234</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/holocaust-survivor-on-very-dangerous-afd-saxony-anhalt-win/a-79278429--2441e4b64e9b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/holocaust-survivor-on-very-dangerous-afd-saxony-anhalt-win/a-79278429?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Charlotte Knobloch survived the Holocaust by passing as the daughter of non-Jewish farmers. She recently spoke with DW to express her shock following the AfD victory in Saxony-Anhalt's state election.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
